# Logging

- When a logger is available in the module or project, log state-changing operations, side effects and one-time surprising behavior (generating a config file, a rollback restoring or deleting files), by default and without being asked.
- Do not log pure reads: getters, accessors and properties.
- Log only what is worth explaining after the fact. Skip messages with no diagnostic value.

Why: a configured logger that nothing calls gives no value, and logging has to be consistent across the codebase, not added only on request.

## Checks
- enforced-by: no-logging-in-property
- enforcement: llm-review
